JSONB OPERATORS




| Execution Order | Clause             | Purpose                                         |
| --------------: | ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |
|               1 | `FROM`             | Identify the source table(s) and perform joins. |
|               2 | `ON`               | Apply join conditions.                          |
|               3 | `JOIN`             | Combine rows from multiple tables.              |
|               4 | `WHERE`            | Filter individual rows.                         |
|               5 | `GROUP BY`         | Group rows based on one or more columns.        |
|               6 | `HAVING`           | Filter groups.                                  |
|               7 | `SELECT`           | Choose the columns/expressions to return.       |
|               8 | `DISTINCT`         | Remove duplicate rows from the result.          |
|               9 | `ORDER BY`         | Sort the result set.                            |
|              10 | `LIMIT` / `OFFSET` | Return only the requested number of rows.       |




